SCOR’s Azure Site Recovery (ASR) architecture strictly mirrors production by provisioning high-cost Premium SSDs for passive replica disks. To eliminate this dormant capacity waste, the ASR Smart Tiering initiative decouples the target storage by utilizing cost-effective Standard HDDs for background replication. Upon triggering a Disaster Recovery (DR) event, an automated runbook seamlessly upgrades the target disks back to Premium SSD before the application boots. This optimization unlocks significant infrastructure savings while guaranteeing zero impact on active production workloads, application performance, or RPO/RTO SLAs.
This Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) provides the step-by-step guidelines for the Production team to retrofit existing ASR environments, deploy the automation, and safely execute DR failovers.
